        new("syntax-schema", "Discover supported concrete AST kinds or the exact typed JSON schema for one kind. ApplicationSyntax.reactionProductionMode is an optional Atomic enum selected by application-root 'reaction batches atomic' (ESM v22); absence retains legacy per-fact semantics even at later versions. Direct and selected refusal-branch production lists are independent atomic batches; invoked commands remain separate. Direct routes and closing constraints remain unadmitted (#770). Consumers must explicitly admit v22. ReactionSyntax.runsAs is an optional init member using ReactionIdentitySyntax; reaction system identity, production routes and observer filters are admitted by released ESM v10; claim conditions evaluate to unknown for it. Clock and application triggers have no Arc realization in Stage yet. Generated values, responses and return expectations are admitted from ESM v7. ConceptSyntax.Generation uses GenerationSyntax; uuid, uuidv7, ulid, typeid, nanoid and bytes are admitted as ESM v15 with exact pinned fixture shapes and Guarded freshness. Pattern, random, implementation generation and String-concept checksum validation are admitted as ESM v21. Pattern dates use one UTC given clock instant for fixture checks, or digit widths only without a clock; suffix arithmetic requires authored validate checksum. Random fixtures are exact integral numbers in an inclusive signed Int64 range. A generation rule requires exactly one direct file or tagged fence and a ValueGeneration requirement with closed Now/Tenant context that the provider binds per target (Cratis C# uses Fundamentals' GenerationContext); reference execution uses fixtures and never invokes its body. sequence is reserved; explicit generation with compliance markers remains refused (#616). Rules on generated concepts select ESM V20, including implicit UUID generated properties: Proven is silent, Refuted is PLAY0688 with a quoted witness, and Unproven is PLAY0689 with a reason. Generated fixtures must satisfy shape and rules; failure is Rejected(Contract), never a redraw. Opaque rules remain Unsupported in reference execution. An explicit unmodified Uuid generate uuid preserves Unguarded behavior and its prior version unless rules select V20; commands using other unadmitted constructs remain unavailable for executable binding. EventSourceSyntax, EventStreamSyntax, EventStreamIdPartSyntax, CommandStreamSyntax and SpecificationStreamSyntax (including streamIdParts), and SpecificationNoStreamSyntax are admitted by ESM v8; property-path mappings and file/inline handlers remain unadmitted (PLAY0268). Pending command handler implementation intents with unconditional produces select ESM v23 (PLAY0695 Information): produces doubles as result contract v1; the body owns payload values, mappings are non-normative, required event properties may be unmapped. No productions or response-only intents refuse binding with PLAY0696; conditional/cardinality-dependent productions refuse with PLAY0697. Consumers must explicitly admit v23. Body-reaching reference execution is Unsupported (ImplementationBody), never a pass. Realization is deferred. Event visibility (public event), event origin (event ... from \"origin\"), Translate slice direction, projection and reducer targets that name an event, and capture source events are admitted by ESM v9; imported public events without a local shape stay refused. Captures over events run from given events and when append, folding incoming properties into per-key state; first arrival is added, unchanged arrivals append nothing. Capture records are refused by PLAY0701 and keys must be required on every from event (PLAY0700). Children and nested scopes over events remain Unsupported. ProducesSyntax.stream replaces the whole command route for that production; ReactionSyntax.from and ReducerSyntax.from select routed facts by source and optional stream, never stream id. These forms are admitted by ESM v10. propose-rename renames sources and streams and repairs command, production, observer and specification routes, leaving pins untouched while migrating catalog entries atomically, including a source's owned streams. Pin the stored name before renaming a declaration with stored events. PropertySyntax.isSubject marks one event property's data subject, is report-only lineage metadata (PLAY0270) and adds no ESM bytes or provider output. PropertySyntax.isKey declares a read-model key; a single explicit key binds byte-identically to inference. Composite read-model keys and QuerySyntax.byParts remain unadmitted with PLAY0268 (#599). ReadsSyntax.byParts is authoring-only like decision reads. propose-property renames and removes explicitly selected non-key command/event/read-model properties along resolved mapping chains; key parts remain unsupported. ConceptSyntax.valueNumbers is an optional init member: absent means positional enum members; populated means unique int32 numbers parallel to values on Enum concepts only. Explicit numbers equal to positions bind byte-identically; other numbers select ESM v12 and bind the optional numbers array parallel to values. Query by keys and supplied filter values satisfy concept rules after authorization in every ESM version; violations reject with Validation, omitted optional filters are not validated. One actionless queried call with one then error and no result, no-result, denial or other outcome selects ESM v18 and asserts exactly Validation. Both when query and then query with arguments use the existing thenQueries and thenErrors members. Consumers must explicitly admit v12; specifications and conditions still name members. propose-number-enum-members pins a wholly unnumbered enum to its current positions. PLAY0671 is an information-level stored-enum hint, not a correctness repair. Concept compliance markers pii/personal and secret select ESM v13, including personal special/criminal qualifiers and secret scope. Reasons remain report-only (PLAY0270). Personal takes precedence over secret; no secret scope is stored next to personal. Compliance on identity or enum concepts is refused. Events combining personal or subject-scoped secret values with an explicit subject mark refuse binding (PLAY0268) until lineage is admitted; subject marks add no ESM bytes. Reference execution is unchanged by compliance; consumers must explicitly admit v13. Caller-supplied equality filters on collection queries select ESM v14: filter names match scalar primitive/concept/enum read-model properties, with matching types ignoring optionality. Optional filters may be omitted; supplied null is refused. Filters combine with by using AND. Context-sourced filters, single-result filters, scoped to and performers remain refused with PLAY0268. Query specifications match collection rows by read model and key without regard to order. Policies still see only by. Consumers must explicitly admit v14. Explicit then no events and when redelivered select ESM v17. No events asserts no new facts from an action and its cascade; after when append the action's fact is excluded. Redelivery locates one given fact and delivers it to only the named reaction without appending it again, then settles the ordinary cascade. Ordered refusal branches and String $refusal.reason, $refusal.constraint and $refusal.message values select ESM v19. The first matching branch handles validation, constraint or explicit authorization refusal and stops the remaining invocations of that trigger; bare refusal excludes authorization. Contract errors, concurrency and Unsupported outcomes never match. Empty branch productions acknowledge; branch append failures end the scenario. Consumers must explicitly admit v17, v18, v19 and v20. Locations and computed members are not editable.", [], ["kind", "offset", "limit"]),
