        new("propose-repair", "Preview one compiler-authored diagnostic repair as a retained, revision-checked typed AST proposal. Discover code and subject with read-workspace view=repairs; review with read-proposal before explicit apply. PLAY0479 migrates optional type spelling with PreserveTrivia, for one occurrence or a document root. PLAY0565 migrates legacy compliance spelling with PreserveTrivia; supply the discovered location line for one concept line, or a document root for all lines. PLAY0653 removes duplicate compliance markers from one concept header with PreserveTrivia, keeping its first markers, body settings and comments. Notes never move. PLAY0516 offers safe timeline sibling moves or explicit pins before a retained glob, including source-only models through a separate syntax/admission proof; its pinned-evidence path is unsupported. Rediscover after each timeline repair. PLAY0563 expands a one-line interaction alternative; PLAY0564 converts a strict item where guard to one when block. Both require individual review, refuse trailing-comment relocation, and do not support pinned evidence. PLAY0614 declares the one translation direction (inbound or outbound) consistent with the slice; it is offered only when exactly one direction fits, requires individual review and does not support pinned evidence. PLAY0661 completes missing named command-read key parts only with unique same-named compatible sources; queries and trigger reads are not repaired, and PLAY0660/PLAY0662 are not supported. PLAY0683/PLAY0684 raise nanoid size or bytes count to at least 64 random bits using the concept subject, even across documents. PLAY0683 also offers a unique constraint using the command-property subject only for exactly one mapped event property. Both require individual review and do not support pinned evidence. PLAY0688 replaces one refuted concept rule with deterministic bounded matches derived from its generation strategy using the concept subject. If generation declares a checksum, the same proposal explicitly adds validate checksum unless already present; this also changes validation of inputs and stored values. Ambiguous or over-budget derived expressions have no repair, with a reason on proposal refusal. It requires individual review and does not support pinned evidence. PLAY0701 replaces a given or when capture record with a given event or when append fixture only when the capture has exactly one from event, preserving its fields. It uses the specification subject, requires individual review and does not support pinned evidence. PLAY0700 needs an authored key decision and has no automatic repair. Other repairs require canonical formatting consent. Canonical reprinting is explicit; comments must survive exactly once. Never writes on discovery or proposal.", ["expectedRevision", "expectedCatalogRevision", "diagnosticCode", "subject", "formatting"], ["expectedRevision", "expectedCatalogRevision", "diagnosticCode", "subject", "formatting", "line", "includeContent", "pinRepairEvidence", "expectedRepairEvidenceRevision"]),
